  "_comment": "SALVAGE kit: cargo-net lashing over a tarped bundle - they carry their loot OUTSIDE. The bundle is a green tarp (the same stolen livery stock the patches are cut from) with a rust lump poking out past one end where the tarp ran short, and the whole thing is YAWED 8 degrees off the plate grid: lashed cargo does not agree with the hull about which way is forward, and that one turn is what keeps a deck of these from tiling. The net is dark straps - three across, one down the length overhanging both ends, two down the flanks - drawn as thin boxes because at cell scale a net reads as its straps. Footprint raised to 0.70 for the yawed diagonal.",
